  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What ingest does",
      "items": [
        "Appends this turn to messages, alternating human and model roles.",
        "It does not query Neo4j, rewrite, or classify the question.",
        "route_question only chooses rewrite_vector, rewrite_graph, or generate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Where memory lives",
      "items": [
        "The notebook uses MemorySaver in RAM. The frontend uses SqliteSaver and a thread_id.",
        "The same id restores messages and documents across turns and restarts.",
        "The client does not resend documents. Deleting a chat deletes the thread. The title is a separate SQLite row."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Router and rewrite window",
      "items": [
        "They see the last eight messages as role and text, plus a digest of ids, names, and counts ranked from 1.",
        "Embeddings and descriptions are left out. “The first one” resolves to a model_id in that digest.",
        "Chat is chosen only when the asked field is already there. An empty history is never chat. With no prior turns, rewrite copies the question."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Anchors, not the graph",
      "items": [
        "generate reads earlier turns and does not repeat the human message just appended.",
        "After retrieval, state holds the question, the rows, and the next follow-up such as “Explain the first one.”",
        "Image-generation models are Hub entities in those rows. This layer does not replace Neo4j."
      ]
    }
  ]
